/-!
# The dispersion bound at `q = 50/33` (this work)

A new exponent, produced from `DispersionGeneral.dispersion_general` by
supplying constants and five `decide`s — no new induction, no new file
of proof script.  Compare `DispersionBound4731`, 92 KB, for the previous
exponent.

The design is the one `DispersionBound4731` uses implicitly, made
explicit: choose `σ = ρ_c(q)^(1/r)` as a rational **rounded up**, so that

  `ρ = σ^r`,  `λ = σ^n = L/D`  are exactly rational,

and the rounding up is what leaves the slack `E = L − D − B ≥ 1` that
absorbs the `+1` of the recursion.  Here `σ = 100691869852/10^11`.
`M` only scales `W`, so it costs nothing in the limit and is taken as
large as the slack needs.

The bound this delivers is

  `c ≥ 2·(2D/L)^(r/n) = 2.517064830151…`

against `2.517064724139…` from `q = 47/31`: the gap to the exact
`2^(1+κ*) = 2.517064836893…` falls from `1.13·10⁻⁷` to `6.7·10⁻⁹`.
-/

